These are COPIES so that a clone of this repo has working gates without the
author's home directory. The knowledge repo above is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
'make check' runs check-vendor, which diffs these files against that source
whenever it is present and FAILS on drift -- so the copy cannot silently rot,
which is the whole cost of vendoring. On a machine without the source (CI), the
check is skipped and says so.

